### Cocos Trading API — example requests
#
# The statement's optional "collection for Postman, Insomnia or REST Client" (research R-023).
# Runs as-is in IntelliJ's HTTP Client and in the VS Code REST Client extension.
#
# Prerequisites: docker compose --profile app up --build
# Expected figures and the reasoning behind them:
#   specs/001-portfolio-endpoint/quickstart.md
# Response contract, enforced by the web tests (ADR-0024):
#   docs/api/openapi.yaml
#
# Only the portfolio endpoint exists so far; instrument search, order submission and
# cancellation get their own sections as those features land.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@userId = 1

### Portfolio — the seeded user
# 200. settledCash 753000.00, availableCash 627500.00 (125500.00 reserved by two BUY LIMIT NEW
# orders), totalAccountValue 889756.00. Positions, ticker ascending: BMA -10 / -15028.00 /
# totalReturnPercent null, METR 500 / 114750.00 / -8.20, PAMP 40 / 37034.00 / -0.45.
# No ARS position: pesos are cash, never a holding.
# Side effect to check in the application log: exactly one ERROR naming BMA and -10 — the seeded
# ledger really does hold a short position, and it is reported rather than hidden (ADR-0012).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/portfolio
Accept: application/json

### Portfolio — a user who has never traded
# 200 with positions [], availableCash 0.00, settledCash 0.00, totalAccountValue 0.00.
# Zeros, not nulls: those values are known (ADR-0013). Users 2, 3 and 4 have no orders in the seed.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/2/portfolio
Accept: application/json

### Portfolio — an id that is not a user
# 404 application/problem+json, title "Not Found", detail "User 999 does not exist".
# Distinguishable from the request above: a wrong id is never served as a real account that has
# never traded (FR-024).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/999/portfolio
Accept: application/json

### Portfolio — a malformed id
# 400 application/problem+json, title "Bad Request", detail
# "Failed to convert 'userId' with value: 'abc'". The id is bound as a long, so this never
# reaches the domain.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/abc/portfolio
Accept: application/json

### Portfolio — two consecutive reads must agree
# Same bytes as the first request, position order included, with no intervening order (SC-006).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}/portfolio
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — an exact ticker
# 200. One result: instrumentId 47, PAMP, Pampa Holding S.A., ACCIONES.
# page 0, size 20 (the configured default), totalElements 1, totalPages 1.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=PAMP
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — the same ticker in lower case
# Identical body: matching folds case on both sides, in SQL (FR-004).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=pamp
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a partial ticker
# Identical results, "query": "pam". Containment, not prefix (FR-003).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=pam
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — surrounding whitespace is trimmed
# Identical body to the request above, with "query": "pamp" (FR-007).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=%20%20pamp%20%20
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — nothing matched is not an error
# 200 with "results": [] and "totalElements": 0. The search ran; nothing matched (FR-011, SC-010).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=ZZZZ
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — cash is never a result
# 200 with an empty page. Pesos are the currency assets are paid in, not a tradable asset, and the
# MONEDA type is excluded (FR-023, ADR-0027). "pesos" is empty for the same reason.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=ars
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a whitespace-only query is rejected
# 400 application/problem+json, detail "The search query must not be blank" (FR-008).
# Contrast with ZZZZ above: there the search ran, here it never did.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=%20%20
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a missing query parameter is rejected
# 400 application/problem+json, detail "Required request parameter 'query' is not present".
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a name fragment returns the family
# 200 with four results, ticker ascending: BBAR, BHIP, BMA, BPAT. All four match on their name
# (FR-002). "BANCO" returns the identical list.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=banco
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — an accented name, typed with its accent
# 200 with one result: MOLI, Molinos Río de la Plata.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=r%C3%ADo
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — the same name, typed without it
# 200 with three results, BHIP, OEST and RICH, and no MOLI: accents are not folded (FR-005,
# ADR-0027). MOLI is still reachable by its ticker or by "molinos".
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=rio
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a typo matches nothing
# 200 with an empty page. "bnaco" is a transposition of "banco"; matching is literal and the API
# does not guess (FR-024).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=bnaco
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — results come in ticker order
# 200 with nine results, ticker ascending (FR-013, FR-014):
#   AGRO  GCLA  GGAL  GRIM  LOMA  MOLA  OEST  PGR  SUPV
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=gr
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a broad query is paged and says how much there is
# 200. page 0, size 20, totalElements 59, totalPages 3, 20 results ending at CVH.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=a
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — the second page
# 200. 20 results, DGCU2 … MOLA. Nothing repeated from page 0, nothing skipped.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=a&page=1
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — the last page
# 200. 19 results, MOLI … YPFD. 20 + 20 + 19 = 59.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=a&page=2
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a page past the last one
# 200 with "results": [] and "totalElements": 59 — an empty page, not an error. An overshooting
# client learns the real total rather than a 404 (FR-015b).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=a&page=3
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — the whole result set in one page
# 200. size 59, totalPages 1, 59 results. A client that wants everything can ask, up to the
# configured maximum.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=a&size=59
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a size above the configured maximum is rejected, not clamped
# 400 application/problem+json, detail "The page size must be between 1 and 100" (FR-015a).
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=a&size=500
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a negative page is rejected
# 400 application/problem+json, detail "The page number must not be negative".
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=a&page=-1
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — an instrument with no price is still an instrument
# 200. instrumentId 3, PGR, with "close": null and "dailyReturnPercent": null — never 0
# (ADR-0013). Prices are looked up after the match, so a missing one cannot drop the instrument.
# PGR and IRCP are the two searchable instruments with no marketdata row.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=pgr
Accept: application/json

### Instrument search — a known zero is a different answer from an unknown one
# 200. AGRO carries "close": 138.00 and "dailyReturnPercent": 0.00 — it closed flat on
# 2023-07-14. Contrast with PGR above, whose figures are null because they are unknown.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/instruments/search?query=agro
Accept: application/json
